- Windows Task Manager now shows automdmd as "AutoMDM" instead of "Orbit osquery runtime and autoupdater", with any AutoMDM server version. App Control for Business (WDAC) rules that match orbit.exe by file description need the new name; the product name stays "AutoMDM osquery".
- **Breaking change:** Once the AutoMDM server is on AutoMDM 5, automdmd renames its Windows Installed apps entry from "AutoMDM osquery" to "AutoMDM", and its Linux process from `orbit` to `automdm`. Service names, the launchd label, the systemd unit, package names, install paths and the installer name don't change. Update policies, scripts and monitoring that look for the name "AutoMDM osquery" on Windows or the process name `orbit` on Linux.
